# Media Workbench v2 — screen comp S1 (⌘E): Effective composite with per-row provenance (conventional, macOS light appearance)
schema: "0.4"
id: mw-screen-styles-composite
type: image
service: gemini
model: gemini-3.1-flash-image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    A straight-on screenshot of a macOS 14 Sonoma app window, light system appearance, SF Pro type, traffic lights, unified toolbar titled "Styles" with a segmented control "Edit | Effective" where "Effective" is selected. The app is a media-generation workbench; this view shows the merged house style for one prompt and which layer won each rule.

    Far left: the translucent source-list sidebar: "Requests 3", "Library", "Runs 2", "Styles" (selected), divider, "Settings".

    Next: the narrow "Layers" pane with four stacked rows, each with a small coloured dot: "House" (grey), "Project · codefre.sh" (blue), "Collection · landing" (purple), "Prompt · pricing-hero" (orange).

    Main area: a header row with a pop-up "Sample: pricing-hero", a small green chip "evalonomi · checksum match", and a muted "sha 3f9a1c".
    Below, a clean table with columns "Rule", "Value", "Layer", "Trail". Each Layer cell is a small rounded tag in that layer's colour. Rows:
    - "palette.accent" · "#FF6B4A" with a coral swatch · tag "Project" · trail "House #C9A227 → Project".
    - "type.headline" · "SF Pro Display Semibold" · tag "House" · trail "—".
    - "voice.tone" · "plain, confident" · tag "Project" · trail "House → Project".
    - "construction.radius" · "12 pt" · tag "Collection" · trail "8 → 10 → 12".
    - "rubric.legibility" · "0.20 required" · tag "House" · trail "—".
    - "rubric.brand-voice" · "0.15 amend" · tag "Project" · trail "House → Project".
    - "rubric.photoreal" · value struck through "suppressed" · tag "Prompt" · trail "House → Prompt".
    One row is selected with a light blue highlight, and a small popover beside it shows a vertical trail of three layer tags with arrows.

    Calm, dense, readable table; left-aligned. Short legible labels and numbers only.
  negative: >
    garbled text, lorem ipsum, watermark, mobile frame, browser chrome, Windows UI,
    perspective tilt, synthesizer/audio-hardware look, CAD tool, manuscript editor,
    dark mode, spreadsheet app, git diff tool, emoji icons, code editor
  style: "UI design screen comp, straight-on screenshot framing, no perspective, no camera tilt, crisp pixel-sharp interface"
output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 95
  dimensions:
    width: 2560
    height: 1600
    aspect_ratio: "16:10"
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    depicts_the_product:
      weight: 0.4
      description: "reads as a media-generation request/review/grading tool, specifically the resolved (effective) brand style for one prompt, showing which style layer won each rule"
    follows_spec:
      weight: 0.35
      description: "shows (1) a composite table of style rules (palette, type, voice, construction, rubric); (2) a winning-layer tag on every row, colour-matched to the layer stack; (3) an override trail per row such as House → Project; (4) a suppressed rubric row and a checksum/source indicator"
    macos_native:
      weight: 0.25
      description: "reads as a native macOS 14 light-appearance window with source list, table, segmented control and popover"
  reject_if:
    - depicts a different product category (spreadsheet, git client, CAD tool, manuscript editor, audio hardware, web page)
    - primary labels (Rule, Layer, row names, layer tags) are unreadable or garbled
tags: [screen-comp, macos, media-workbench, v2]
